# Common unit spellings get a targeted hint.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where duration > 10min
---- expected
IDENT@0..1 "t"
WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
PIPE@2..3 "|"
WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
IDENT@4..9 "where"
WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
IDENT@10..18 "duration"
WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
GT@19..20 ">"
WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
TIMESPAN@21..26 "10min"
WHITESPACE@26..27 "\n"

error[DS0003]: unknown timespan unit `min`
  --> query:1:24
  |
1 | t | where duration > 10min
  |                        ^^^ not a timespan unit
  |
  = help: valid units are `d`, `h`, `m` (minutes), `s`, `ms`, `us` (or `µs`) and `tick` (100 ns)
  = help: for minutes, write `m`: `30m`
